diff --git a/docs/events.md b/docs/events.md
index 80189d4..4a0962f 100644
--- a/docs/events.md
+++ b/docs/events.md
@@ -1,7 +1,25 @@
 # Event stream
 
-Clients connect to `/v1/events` and receive every event as it is published.
+Clients connect to `/v1/events?cursor=<seq>` and first receive every
+retained event with `seq > cursor`, then live events as they are published.
 
 ## Ordering
 
-Events carry a monotonically increasing `seq`.
+Events carry a strictly increasing `seq`. Clients should remember the last
+`seq` they processed and pass it as `cursor` when reconnecting.
+
+## Backpressure
+
+The daemon never blocks on a slow client:
+
+- Live delivery uses a bounded broadcast channel (4096 events).
+- A client that falls further behind is **lagged**: the daemon replays the
+  missed events from the store and continues live.
+- If the missed events have already aged out of the store, the client
+  receives what is retained and should refetch snapshots over REST.
+
+| Situation | Daemon behaviour |
+| --- | --- |
+| Client keeps up | Live events only |
+| Client lags | Resync from store, then live |
+| Store evicted gap | Partial replay; client refetches |
